**Given:**

Selling price (SP) = ₹237

Gain = 18.5%

**Formula used:**

Cost Price (CP) = dfrac{SP}{1 + (Gain\%)/(100)}

**Calculation:**

CP = dfrac{237}{1 + (18.5)/(100)}

⇒ CP = dfrac{237}{1 + 0.185}

⇒ CP = dfrac{237}{1.185}

⇒ CP = ₹200

**∴ The correct answer is option 1.**
